{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779230433,"nonce":"81EP2m0yb7wS90eECZidGjn762M=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCx-uYw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/141","origin":"github"},"title":"Remove diagnostic_aggregator from operator launches (annunciator uses /diagnostics directly)","message":"## Observation\n\n`/diagnostics_agg` on the operator station declares four `/Operator/*` rollup buckets that are all **STALE**:\n\n- `/Operator/MikroTik`\n- `/Operator/Ping`\n- `/Operator/Starlink`\n- `/Operator/Teltonika`\n\nDocumented in salmon log §10 + §12 of the [2026-05-19 deployment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135).\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe real publishers — operator-side `mikrotik_monitor`, `ping_monitor`, `starlink_diagnostics`, `teltonika_monitor` — publish their `DiagnosticStatus` entries under `/Other/...` (e.g., `/Other/ping_monitor: ping.op: ...`, `/Other/mikrotik_monitor: wifi.bizzy: ...`), not under `/Operator/...`.\n\nThe diagnostics aggregator config still expects `/Operator/*` paths and finds nothing → all 4 buckets STALE. Pre-existing config drift, not introduced today.\n\n## Independent of #3 / `ros2_network_monitor#23`\n\nEven if the operator-side `mikrotik_monitor` + `teltonika_monitor` weren't crashing on startup ([ros2_network_monitor#23](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/23)), the `/Operator/*` buckets would still be STALE because the aggregator's path map is wrong. The `starlink_diagnostics` and `ping_monitor` bucket entries are stale right now despite those two monitors being alive and publishing.\n\n## Fix options\n\n1. **Update the aggregator path map** — point `/Operator/MikroTik` etc. at the actual `/Other/{mikrotik,teltonika,starlink,ping}_monitor: *` paths. Smallest change.\n2. **Rename the aggregator buckets** to `/Other/*` style so they match where publishers land. Equivalent to dropping the `/Operator/*` rollup and relying on `/Other`.\n3. **Relocate publishers** to publish under `/Operator/*` directly. Bigger change; touches `ros2_network_monitor`. Probably overkill unless there's a wider intent to namespace operator-side diagnostics.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Toplevel `/diagnostics_agg` is driven to STALE/ERROR by these dead buckets, masking real warnings/errors elsewhere.\n- Operator loses faith in the toplevel summary when it's always wrong — they have to drill down every time.\n\n## Repo\n\n`unh_echoboats_project11` — where the BizzyBoat diagnostics_aggregator config lives (`bizzyboat_project11/config/...`).\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}